select 'thermo-kinetics-equilibrium', 'Le Chatelier''s principle: Thermodynamic statement', 'The Le Chatelier–Braun principle analyzes the qualitative behaviour of a thermodynamic system when a particular one of its externally controlled state variables, say all other externally controlled state variables remaining constant. The response illustrates ''moderation'' in ways evident in two related thermodynamic equilibria. Also as a necessary part of the scenario, there is some particular auxiliary ''moderating'' state variable in some part of the experimental protocol; this can be either by imposition of a change is so. To give this scenario physical meaning, the ''driving'' variable and the ''moderating'' variable must be subject to separate independent experimental controls and measurements.', 'Wikipedia: Le Chatelier''s principle', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Le_Chatelier''s_principle&oldid=1366339970', 'CC BY-SA 4.0. Wikipedia contributors (see page history). Excerpted and split into passages.'
